proof.text:
The object constructions give dg functors. On a homogeneous degree-$r$ map $u$, use $F(u)(b\otimes n)=(-1)^{r|b|}b\otimes u(n)$ and $G(u)=f_*u$ degreewise. The balancing check is the one in step 2. Composition adds the exponents, so identities and compositions are preserved. For $p=|b|$, expansion gives
$\delta(Fu)(b\otimes n)=(-1)^{rp+p}b\otimes(d u-(-1)^r u d)(n)=F(\delta u)(b\otimes n)$;
the two $d(b)\otimes u(n)$ terms cancel because $r+r(p+1)\equiv rp$ modulo $2$. Sectionwise the same identity for $G$ is immediate. In particular $F,G$ take chain maps to chain maps. Their object differentials square to zero: the two mixed tensor terms cancel, and balancing is preserved since differentiating $b\varphi(c)\otimes n=b\otimes cn$ gives the same terms using the Leibniz rules and $d\varphi=\varphi d$.
